      "source": "Design (EN)",
      "title": "Overall purpose",
      "content": "This module aims to **coordinate the two engineered strains through naringenin signaling** and **link wound heme sensing to downstream functional protein expression**.\n\nOur project divides environmental sensing and functional protein production between two engineered bacterial species. Their coordination requires the sender to convert an environmental cue into a signal that the receiver can detect. We propose a communication pathway in which *Staphylococcus epidermidis* produces naringenin in response to heme. The receiver, *Escherichia coli* Nissle 1917 (EcN), senses naringenin and activates downstream gene expression. This pathway is designed to provide a controllable input for the wound-healing promotion module.[12–16]\n\n| Module | Full name | Role in the design |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| HmSr | Heme Sensor | Detects heme in the sender and controls downstream gene expression. |\n| Nr | Naringenin Biosynthesis Module | Synthesizes naringen",
