      "title": "Gene organization and plasmid construction",
      "content": "#### Sender: independent sensing and synthesis constructs\n\nTwo separate sender constructs, HmSr–sfGFP and constitutive pcap–Nr, use the pBUS1 backbone. In HmSr–sfGFP, pHrtBA drives sfGFP expression to characterize the response to heme. In pcap–Nr, the constitutive promoter pcap drives At4CL, PhCHS, and CmCHI expression to test the biosynthetic pathway independently. Both constructs retain the pBUS1 replication origin and ampicillin and tetracycline resistance markers.\n\nThe proposed HmSr–Nr construct places the three-enzyme pathway under pHrtBA control to couple heme sensing to naringenin production. The host supplies the native HssS and HssR proteins for heme sensing.\n\n**Figure 6 | Proposed HmSr–Nr sender construct.**\n\n#### Receiver: reporter-based characterization of the naringenin response\n\nNrSr–sfGFP uses a pUC19-derived backbone that retains the replication origin and ampicillin resistance marker. We designed the receiver circuit us",
