      "content": "lso the receiver Results.\n\n#### Supernatant transfer: matching sender output to the receiver's response range\n\nIn subsequent experiments, we will add sterile-filtered supernatant from Nr sender cultures to NrSr–sfGFP receiver cells. Controls will include supernatants from senders cultured without precursor or lacking the Nr pathway, matched medium, and supernatant supplemented with a known amount of naringenin. The supplemented supernatant will test whether the culture supernatant affects the receiver's response to naringenin.\n\nAfter confirming naringenin identity and measuring its concentration, we will calculate the final concentration following dilution in the receiver culture. We will compare this concentration with the NrSr response range and measure receiver fluorescence to determine whether sender output is sufficient to induce a response. These controls will help distinguish insufficient naringenin production from effects of the",
