      "id": "D145",
      "source": "Design (EN)",
      "title": "Gene Organization & Plasmid Construction",
      "content": "The responsive construct, **NrSr–PelB–LSp222**, uses a pUC19-derived backbone with its replication origin and ampicillin resistance marker.\n\nThe bidirectional regulatory region **PfdeAR** contains two oppositely oriented promoters. **PfdeR** drives the *fdeR* gene encoding the naringenin-responsive regulator FdeR, while **PfdeA** drives the downstream output (Figure 9).[12,13] For this regulatory system, see the dual-species communication module.\n\nBuilding on the NrSr–sfGFP construct used to characterize the receiver, the antibacterial construct retains FdeR and its bidirectional regulatory region. The reporter output downstream of PfdeA is replaced with `B0034–pelB–mature LSp222–6×His–B0015`. B0034 is the ribosome binding site (RBS), the 6×His tag supports detection and purification, and B0015 is the transcriptional terminator.\n\nWe also inserted the same mature protein fragment into pET-22b by restriction enzyme cloning to establish an",
