      "title": "Overall Purpose",
      "content": "naringenin synthesis module (Nr) in the upstream *S. epidermidis* sender to provide EcN with a signal for the transition between stages.[16]\n\nThe key requirements are naringenin-regulated protein expression and extracellular release. Regulated expression allows hEGF output to vary with the input signal, while extracellular release allows the repair factor to reach wound tissue from the receiver cells. Coordination between treatment stages and the repair effect will be evaluated progressively as system-level design goals.\n\n**Figure 10 | hEGF module design overview.**",
      "tags": "S4 B2 B4 B9 B10 B1 B3 X05 naringenin HPLC yield supernatant 400 7.32 14.65 53.8 柚皮素 产量 上清 发酵液 标曲 S4 B2 B4 B11 B1 X01 X03 X04 X08 EcN receiver NrSr FdeR PfdeAR negative fluorescence dose response 接收端 负荧光 基底泄漏 S5 S6 B2 B4 B14 B1 X10 hEGF PelB two bands doublet 11.10 8.89 kDa supernatant 两个条带 双条带 信号肽 上清 促愈合"
