      "source": "Design (EN)",
      "title": "Component Selection and Rationale",
      "content": "We selected mature hEGF as the repair output based on its known role in wound healing. A clinical trial in diabetic foot ulcers reported improved granulation and wound closure following local injection of recombinant hEGF.[26] Using mature hEGF focuses the construct on the active protein region.\n\nThe PelB signal peptide directs newly synthesized protein to the *E. coli* periplasm. Previous work used this route to express hEGF and detected the product in culture supernatant.[27] We therefore place PelB at the N terminus of mature hEGF, using periplasmic targeting as the starting point for evaluating extracellular release.\n\nNrSr converts naringenin input into gene expression. We selected EcN for the final signal response and repair output, and use BL21(DE3) for initial protein expression tests so that signal reception and protein output can be validated separately.",
      "tags": "S4 B2 B4 B9 B10 B1 B3 X05 naringenin HPLC yield supernatant 400 7.32 14.65 53.8 柚皮素 产量 上清 发酵液 标曲 S4 B2 B4 B11 B1 X01 X03 X04 X08 EcN receiver NrSr FdeR PfdeAR negative fluorescence dose response 接收端 负荧光 基底泄漏 S5 S6 B2 B4 B14 B1 X10 hEGF PelB two bands doublet 11.10 8.89 kDa supernatant 两个条带 双条带 信号肽 上清 促愈合 S1 S6 B4 X12 X13 biosafety D-alanine auxotrophy hydrogel 40 um escape 生物安全 活菌逃逸 水凝胶 营养缺陷"
