      "content": "The final responsive construct, **NrSr–PelB–hEGF**, uses a pUC19-derived backbone with its replication origin and ampicillin resistance marker.\n\n**PfdeAR**, the bidirectional regulatory region of NrSr, contains two oppositely oriented promoters: **PfdeR** drives the *fdeR* gene encoding the naringenin-responsive regulator FdeR, and **PfdeA** drives the downstream output (Figure 11). For this regulatory system, see the dual-species communication module.[12,13]\n\nBuilding on the NrSr–sfGFP construct used to characterize the receiver, the wound-healing construct retains FdeR and its bidirectional regulatory region and replaces the reporter output downstream of PfdeA with `B0034–pelB–mature hEGF–6×His–B0015`.\n\nB0034 is the ribosome binding site (RBS) for translation initiation; pelB and mature hEGF remain in the same reading frame; the 6×His tag supports detection and purification; and B0015 is the terminator.[28,29] The RBS and terminator s",
