      "content": "Uninduced fluorescence increased over time, and weak cell-associated signals remained visible in microscopy. Basal output therefore matters when the receiver is connected to an active protein such as LSp222. Its effect should be evaluated with the protein output and target cells of interest.\n\nThe two hosts were tested in separate batches, with a fixed same-host fluorescence background measured later. That correction can yield negative early values and does not include the uncertainty of the background estimate. The BL21(DE3) culture setup also changed at 16 h. Plateau estimates at low input remain weakly constrained.",
